{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/b1-explainer-about-people-using-adderall-and-other-non-natural-ways-to-perform-better-at-s/audio/main-904933baa845.mp3","durationSec":249.696,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":6.48,"text":"A study drug is a medicine used with the aim of improving concentration, energy, or academic performance."},{"start":7.54,"end":9.82,"text":"Adderall is a well-known example in the United States."},{"start":10.56,"end":17.76,"text":"It contains mixed amphetamine salts and is prescribed mainly for attention deficit hyperactivity disorder, or ADHD."},{"start":18.92,"end":24.22,"text":"It can help a person with ADHD manage symptoms such as poor attention and impulsive behavior."},{"start":25,"end":29.6,"text":"However, some people without ADHD take Adderall without medical advice."},{"start":30.52,"end":33.2,"text":"They may hope to study all night or finish more work."},{"start":34.28,"end":39.66,"text":"It is useful to separate three points: the source, the change, and the result."},{"start":40.6,"end":47.62,"text":"The source is the drug, the change may be greater alertness, and the hoped-for result is better performance."},{"start":48.8,"end":52.42,"text":"Stimulants can make a person feel awake, energetic, or confident."},{"start":53.04,"end":58.04,"text":"However, this feeling does not always mean that the person is learning more effectively."},{"start":58.04,"end":63.22,"text":"Complex learning requires understanding, memory, judgment, and enough sleep."},{"start":64.2,"end":67.38,"text":"A student may work for many hours but remember little the next day."},{"start":68.2,"end":69.54,"text":"There are also health risks."},{"start":70.34,"end":74.78,"text":"Adderall can cause sleep problems, anxiety, a fast heartbeat, and loss of appetite."},{"start":75.76,"end":78.1,"text":"Using too much can lead to more serious harm."},{"start":78.86,"end":81.14,"text":"It can also become habit-forming."},{"start":81.14,"end":89.44,"text":"The source-change-result lens helps here: a stimulant may change alertness, but the final result can include poor sleep and weaker performance later."},{"start":89.44,"end":96.48,"text":"Medical supervision matters because a doctor considers the person’s condition, dose, and other medicines."},{"start":97.92,"end":103.96,"text":"Taking a prescribed medicine for a diagnosed condition is different from using someone else’s medicine to gain an advantage."},{"start":105.18,"end":110.76,"text":"A doctor may prescribe a stimulant after evaluating ADHD symptoms and checking the patient’s health."},{"start":111.04,"end":113.82,"text":"The doctor can then monitor benefits and side effects."},{"start":113.82,"end":117.5,"text":"Non-medical use has no such safety process."},{"start":118.3,"end":121.98,"text":"A pill bought online or received from a friend may have the wrong dose."},{"start":122.7,"end":127.8,"text":"It may even be counterfeit, meaning that it is made to look real but contains unknown substances."},{"start":128.7,"end":131.7,"text":"Sharing prescription medicine is also illegal in many places."},{"start":131.7,"end":134.2,"text":"Questions of fairness can arise too."},{"start":134.9,"end":139.56,"text":"Some people compare study drugs to cheating, while others compare them to strong coffee."},{"start":140.18,"end":144.98,"text":"The important differences are medical need, risk, access, and professional supervision."},{"start":145.84,"end":153.68,"text":"Adderall is strongly associated with the United States, but it is not a routine ADHD medicine in China or South Korea."},{"start":153.68,"end":158.08,"text":"Amphetamine-based drugs face strict legal controls in both countries."},{"start":158.66,"end":165.26,"text":"Methylphenidate, another prescription stimulant, may be used to treat ADHD, but access and prescribing rules are controlled."},{"start":166.2,"end":172.62,"text":"Bringing medication across a border can also require official permission, even when a traveler has a prescription from another country."},{"start":173.46,"end":179.54,"text":"China’s gaokao and South Korea’s College Scholastic Ability Test are famous high-pressure entrance exams."},{"start":180.32,"end":184.52,"text":"This pressure can encourage long study hours, but it does not mean that all students use drugs."},{"start":185.54,"end":190.76,"text":"More common performance aids include coffee, tea, energy drinks, supplements, and sleep reduction."},{"start":191.78,"end":195.82,"text":"Individual behavior varies greatly, so national stereotypes are not helpful."},{"start":195.82,"end":199.46,"text":"Performance-enhancing behavior is not only about one drug."},{"start":199.46,"end":204.82,"text":"It is also connected to competition, long working hours, fear of failure, and limited support."},{"start":205.26,"end":213.02,"text":"A student preparing for the gaokao or the South Korean entrance exam may sleep less because the exam feels extremely important."},{"start":214.38,"end":218.92,"text":"An employee facing a difficult deadline may depend on several energy drinks."},{"start":220,"end":224.92,"text":"These choices have different legal and medical risks, but they can come from similar pressure."},{"start":225.42,"end":229.1,"text":"A helpful response should therefore include both safety and environment."},{"start":229.8,"end":237.46,"text":"People need accurate information about medicines, confidential medical support, realistic schedules, sleep, and fair expectations."},{"start":238.32,"end":243.12,"text":"If someone is struggling to concentrate, professional assessment is safer than borrowing a pill."},{"start":244.06,"end":249.1,"text":"Improving the conditions around performance can reduce the desire for a quick chemical solution."}],"words":[{"text":"A","start":0,"end":0.14},{"text":"study","start":0.14,"end":0.42},{"text":"drug","start":0.42,"end":0.8},{"text":"is","start":0.8,"end":1.16},{"text":"a","start":1.16,"end":1.26},{"t